#
# The site moved to mixtape.niels-lazaroms.nl. Netlify stays alive purely to
# forward the QR codes already printed against the old address, so it no longer
# serves the app: it hands every request straight on, path and query intact, so
# a card link like /?t=<id> still lands in the right round.
#
# The trailing ! forces the rule even though index.html exists in the output;
# without it Netlify would serve the file and never redirect. 301 because the
# move is settled and the printed codes are permanent: a browser that has
# scanned once then skips this hop entirely. The cost is that the destination
# is now cached, so moving the app again means stale redirects for anyone who
# has been here before.
